 Total Energy = E(Solvent-Solvent) + ESX + EXX + E(phi) + E-Bond + E-Bend + ENB + ECUT + E(Internal Solvent)
 ESX = The Solute-Solvent Energy
 EXX = The Solute-Solute Energy
 E(phi) = The Torsional Energy for the Solutes
 E-Bond = The Bond Stretching Energy for the Solutes
 E-Bend = The Angle Bending Energy for the Solutes
 ENB = The Intrasolute >1,3-nonbonded Energy
 E-BCON = The Harmonic Distance Constraints Energy (in EXX)
 E(AM1) or E(PM3) = QM Energy for the Solutes
 ECUT= The Cutoff Correction to the Solvent-Solvent Energy for Non-aqueous Solvents (L-J Only)
